def marketplace():
    S=[('supply-demand-mkt','Marketplace Supply and Demand',['economics.supply-demand','math.equations'],22,'The Marketplace price system follows supply and demand laws that need analysis.',_4step('observe','Survey buyer willingness-to-pay and seller willingness-to-accept for three goods.','Record data at five different price levels.','build','Plot supply and demand curves from the survey data.','Price on y-axis, quantity on x-axis.','solve','Find the equilibrium price and quantity where curves intersect.','The intersection balances buyers and sellers.','predict','Predict the new equilibrium if supply increases by 20%.','Shift the supply curve right and find the new intersection.')),
    ('business-plan','Business Plan Development',['economics.entrepreneurship','math.equations'],22,'New Marketplace businesses need financial planning based on mathematical projections.',_4step('design','Outline a business plan with product, target market, and revenue model.','Identify what the business sells and to whom.','solve','Calculate startup costs, monthly expenses, and projected monthly revenue.','List every cost category and revenue source.','solve','Calculate the break-even point: when cumulative revenue exceeds cumulative costs.','Break-even month = total startup costs / monthly net revenue.','predict','Project profit or loss for the first year of operation.','Sum all monthly revenues and subtract all costs.')),
    ('interest-savings','Savings Account Interest',['economics.banking','math.equations'],22,'Marketplace bank accounts earn compound interest that needs calculation.',_4step('solve','Calculate the balance after 1 year on 1000 coins at 5% annual interest.','Balance = 1000 times (1 + 0.05) = 1050.','solve','Calculate the balance after 5 years with annual compounding.','Balance = 1000 times (1.05)^5.','compare','Compare annual vs monthly compounding for the same rate and time.','Monthly compounding: Balance = 1000 times (1 + 0.05/12)^(12*5).','predict','Predict the balance after 20 years and appreciate the power of compound interest.','Balance = 1000 times (1.05)^20 = about 2653 coins.')),
    ('credit-debt','Credit and Debt Management',['economics.credit','math.equations'],22,'Marketplace merchants must understand credit, interest charges, and debt management.',_4step('solve','Calculate the monthly interest charge on a 500-coin balance at 18% annual rate.','Monthly rate = 18% / 12 = 1.5%; charge = 500 times 0.015 = 7.50.','solve','Calculate how long to pay off the debt making minimum payments of 25 coins per month.','Each payment reduces principal by payment minus interest charge.','compare','Compare total interest paid under minimum payments vs paying double.','Paying more each month dramatically reduces total interest.','predict','Calculate the total cost of the 500-coin purchase including all interest charges.','Sum all payments over the payoff period.')),
    ('markup-discount-mkt','Markup and Discount Chains',['math.percentages','economics.entrepreneurship'],18,'Marketplace pricing involves chains of markups and discounts that need careful calculation.',_4step('solve','Apply a 60% markup to a wholesale cost of 50 coins.','Selling price = 50 times 1.60 = 80 coins.','solve','Apply a 25% seasonal discount to the 80-coin marked price.','Sale price = 80 times 0.75 = 60 coins.','solve','Calculate the net profit or loss compared to the original 50-coin cost.','Net = selling price - cost = 60 - 50 = 10 coins profit.','predict','Calculate the minimum markup needed to stay profitable after a planned 30% discount.','After discount: cost times (1+markup) times 0.70 must exceed cost.')),
    ('elasticity','Price Elasticity of Demand',['economics.supply-demand','math.equations'],22,'Some goods are more price-sensitive than others and elasticity measures this.',_4step('measure','Record quantity demanded at two different prices for three goods.','Note the percentage change in price and quantity for each.','solve','Calculate price elasticity: % change in quantity / % change in price.','Elasticity greater than 1 means demand is elastic (price-sensitive).','compare','Classify each good as elastic, inelastic, or unit elastic.','Necessities tend to be inelastic; luxuries tend to be elastic.','predict','Predict the revenue effect of a 10% price increase for each good.','Elastic goods: revenue decreases; inelastic goods: revenue increases.')),
    ('profit-loss','Profit and Loss Statements',['economics.entrepreneurship','math.equations'],20,'Marketplace businesses track profit and loss to measure financial health.',_4step('collect','Record all revenue and expense items for a business over one month.','Categorize each item as revenue, cost of goods, or operating expense.','solve','Calculate gross profit: revenue minus cost of goods sold.','Gross profit = total revenue - cost of goods.','solve','Calculate net profit: gross profit minus operating expenses.','Net profit = gross profit - all other expenses.','compare','Compare profit margins across three different Marketplace businesses.','Profit margin = net profit / revenue times 100.')),
    ('unit-rate-shopping','Unit Rate Comparison Shopping',['math.ratios','economics.supply-demand'],18,'Marketplace shoppers need unit rates to compare differently-sized packages.',_4step('solve','Calculate the unit price of three differently-sized packages of the same product.','Unit price = total price / quantity or weight.','compare','Identify which package size offers the best value.','The lowest unit price is the best value per unit.','solve','Calculate the savings from buying the best-value package vs the most expensive.','Savings = (expensive unit price - cheapest unit price) times quantity.','predict','Predict whether a buy-one-get-one-half-off deal is better than the bulk price.','Calculate the effective unit price of the deal.')),
    ('linear-revenue','Revenue Modeling',['math.linear-functions','economics.entrepreneurship'],20,'Revenue follows a linear pattern with price as the variable.',_4step('collect','Record revenue at five different price points.','Note both price and resulting revenue.','solve','Plot revenue vs price and check for a linear region.','Revenue may be linear over a limited price range.','solve','Find the linear equation: Revenue = a times price + b.','Use two data points to solve for a and b.','predict','Predict revenue at a price not yet tested.','Substitute the new price into the equation.')),
    ('statistics-sales-mkt','Sales Data Statistics',['math.statistics','economics.market-structures'],18,'Marketplace sales data needs statistical analysis for inventory and pricing decisions.',_4step('collect','Record daily sales quantities for a product over 20 days.','Note exact sales count each day.','solve','Calculate mean, median, mode, and standard deviation.','These describe central tendency and variability.','compare','Identify the busiest and slowest days and any patterns.','Look for day-of-week or other cyclical patterns.','predict','Predict next week sales based on statistical patterns.','Use the mean adjusted for any day-of-week effects.')),
    ('proportion-recipe','Recipe Scaling for Production',['math.proportions','math.ratios'],18,'Marketplace food vendors must scale recipes proportionally for different batch sizes.',_4step('solve','Scale a recipe serving 4 to serve 25.','Multiply each ingredient by 25/4 = 6.25.','solve','Scale a recipe down from serving 50 to serving 12.','Multiply each ingredient by 12/50 = 0.24.','measure','Prepare the scaled recipe and verify the proportions taste correct.','Proportional scaling should maintain the same flavor profile.','predict','Calculate ingredient costs for the scaled batch.','Multiply each ingredient cost by the scaling factor.')),
    ('coordinate-market-map','Market Floor Coordinate System',['math.coordinate-geometry','engineering.design-process'],18,'The Marketplace floor uses coordinates for stall assignment and navigation.',_4step('design','Set up a coordinate grid over the Marketplace with the main gate as origin.','Align axes with the main aisles.','place','Assign coordinate positions to 15 vendor stalls.','Record x,y for each stall location.','solve','Calculate the distance between the most popular stalls.','Use the distance formula.','optimize','Propose a new layout that minimizes average walking distance between popular stalls.','Try different arrangements and calculate average distances.')),
    ('equations-cost','Cost Equation Systems',['math.equations','economics.entrepreneurship'],20,'Business cost structures follow equations that can predict expenses at different production levels.',_4step('solve','Write the total cost equation: TC = FC + VC times Q where FC is fixed, VC is variable per unit.','Identify the fixed and variable components.','solve','Calculate total cost for producing 100, 200, and 500 units.','Substitute each quantity into the equation.','solve','Find the break-even quantity where revenue equals total cost.','Set price times Q = FC + VC times Q and solve for Q.','predict','Predict the profit at a production level of 300 units.','Profit = Revenue - Total Cost at Q = 300.')),
    ('pythagorean-display','Display Diagonal Sizing',['math.pythagorean-theorem','math.geometry'],18,'Marketplace display stands need diagonal calculations for proper signage fitting.',_4step('measure','Measure the width and height of a rectangular display frame.','Record both dimensions.','solve','Calculate the frame diagonal using the Pythagorean theorem.','Diagonal = sqrt(width^2 + height^2).','solve','Determine the maximum sign size that fits within the frame.','The sign must fit within the diagonal constraint.','predict','Predict the frame dimensions needed for a sign of specific diagonal size.','Use the desired aspect ratio with the diagonal constraint.')),
    ('percentage-tax-mkt','Sales Tax Calculations',['math.percentages','economics.market-structures'],18,'The Marketplace charges sales tax that must be calculated correctly on every transaction.',_4step('solve','Calculate 7% sales tax on a 85-coin purchase.','Tax = 85 times 0.07 = 5.95 coins.','solve','Calculate the total price including tax.','Total = 85 + 5.95 = 90.95 coins.','solve','Calculate the pre-tax price if the total including 7% tax is 107 coins.','Pre-tax = 107 / 1.07 = 100 coins.','compare','Compare total tax paid by different customers with different purchase patterns.','More expensive purchases generate more tax revenue.')),
    ('probability-sales','Sales Probability Forecasting',['math.probability','math.statistics'],18,'The Marketplace uses probability to forecast demand and manage inventory.',_4step('collect','Record daily demand for a product over 30 days.','Note exact units demanded each day.','solve','Create a probability distribution from the demand data.','P(demand = x) = days with demand x / 30.','predict','Calculate the expected daily demand.','Expected value = sum of (x times P(x)) for each demand level.','solve','Determine the stock level needed to satisfy demand on 90% of days.','Find the demand level at the 90th percentile.')),
    ('exponents-growth','Business Growth Modeling',['math.exponents','economics.entrepreneurship'],20,'Marketplace businesses grow at rates that can be modeled with exponents.',_4step('collect','Record monthly revenue for a growing business over 12 months.','Note the revenue for each month.','solve','Model the growth as exponential: Revenue = R0 times (1+rate)^month.','Find the rate from the ratio of consecutive months.','solve','Calculate the doubling time for the business revenue.','Doubling time = ln(2) / ln(1+rate).','predict','Project revenue 12 months into the future using the growth model.','Substitute month 24 into the equation.')),
    ('scientific-notation-mkt','Large Transaction Notation',['math.scientific-notation','economics.gdp'],18,'Some Marketplace transactions involve very large numbers needing scientific notation.',_4step('transform','Express a trade deal worth 45,000,000 coins in scientific notation.','4.5 x 10^7 coins.','solve','Calculate the daily average from a yearly total of 1.2 x 10^9 coins.','Divide by 365: approximately 3.3 x 10^6 coins per day.','compare','Express individual transaction values alongside annual totals.','Show the scale difference between single sales and yearly revenue.','solve','Calculate the commission on a large deal at 2.5% of 4.5 x 10^7.','0.025 times 4.5 x 10^7 = 1.125 x 10^6.')),
    ('coding-pos','Point of Sale System',['cs.functions','cs.data-structures'],22,'The Marketplace needs a point-of-sale program for processing transactions.',_4step('code','Write a function that calculates subtotal from item prices and quantities.','Sum price times quantity for each item.','code','Add functions for tax calculation and total with payment processing.','Apply tax rate and compute change from payment.','code','Create a receipt generator that lists all items, subtotal, tax, and total.','Format each line with item, quantity, price, and line total.','experiment','Process 10 test transactions and verify all calculations.','Check subtotals, tax, totals, and change amounts.')),
    ('coding-inventory','Inventory Management System',['cs.data-structures','cs.functions'],22,'The Marketplace inventory needs a program for tracking stock levels and reordering.',_4step('code','Design a data structure for inventory items with name, stock, minimum, and reorder quantity.','Each item tracks current stock and when to reorder.','code','Write a function that updates stock after sales and receives.','Subtract sold quantities; add received quantities.','code','Create a reorder report listing items below their minimum stock level.','Filter items where current stock is below minimum.','experiment','Simulate two weeks of sales and restocking and verify the system tracks correctly.','Check stock levels after each day of simulation.')),
    ]
    ST=[('machine-mkt-predictor','Machine Fragment: Market Predictor',['economics.supply-demand','math.probability'],22,'An ancient device predicts market prices days in advance with extraordinary accuracy.',_4step('observe','Record the device price predictions for five goods over one week.','Note predicted vs actual prices each day.','measure','Calculate the prediction accuracy rate and average error.','Accuracy = correct predictions / total; error = |predicted - actual|.','compare','Compare device accuracy to modern market forecasting models.','Note the lead time and accuracy advantages.','experiment','Test whether the device predictions remain accurate during unusual market conditions.','Create supply shocks and check if predictions adapt.')),
    ('machine-mkt-scales','Machine Fragment: Fair Scales',['physics.forces','economics.supply-demand'],22,'Ancient scales automatically adjust to give a fair price for any goods placed on them.',_4step('experiment','Place various goods on the scales and record the indicated prices.','Test with common and rare items.','compare','Compare the scale prices to current market prices.','Note which items the scales price higher or lower than the market.','solve','Analyze the pricing algorithm by testing goods of known value.','Look for patterns in how the scales determine value.','measure','Test whether the scales factor in condition, rarity, and quality.','Place items of varying quality and note price differences.')),
    ('machine-mkt-ledger','Machine Fragment: Perfect Ledger',['cs.data-structures','economics.banking'],22,'An ancient ledger system tracks every transaction in the Marketplace automatically.',_4step('observe','Conduct transactions and check if the ledger records them automatically.','Note accuracy, speed, and detail of the automatic entries.','measure','Determine the maximum distance at which transactions are recorded.','Conduct trades at increasing distances.','compare','Compare the ledger accuracy and speed to modern accounting software.','Note any advantages in automation or error prevention.','experiment','Test whether the ledger detects and flags suspicious transactions.','Conduct unusual transactions and check for alerts.')),
    ('machine-mkt-negotiator','Machine Fragment: Fair Price Crystal',['economics.market-structures','math.equations'],22,'An ancient crystal glows at the mathematically fair price for any negotiation.',_4step('experiment','Present different negotiation scenarios and record the crystal indicated price.','Try buyer-favored, seller-favored, and balanced scenarios.','solve','Calculate the theoretical fair price from available market data.','Fair price often means the price where both parties gain equally.','compare','Compare the crystal price to the Nash bargaining solution.','The Nash solution maximizes the product of both parties gains.','measure','Test whether the crystal accounts for information asymmetry.','Give one party more information and check if the indicated price changes.')),
    ('machine-mkt-transport','Machine Fragment: Instant Transport',['physics.forces','engineering.mechanisms'],22,'An ancient device moves goods instantly between two locations without physical transit.',_4step('experiment','Place items at the source and check if they appear at the destination.','Test with different item types and sizes.','measure','Determine the maximum weight and size the device can transport.','Gradually increase load until transport fails.','compare','Compare transport speed and cost to conventional shipping.','Conventional shipping takes time and fuel; this is instant.','solve','Calculate the economic impact of zero-time transport on trade patterns.','Consider how eliminating shipping time affects supply chains.')),
    ('machine-mkt-quality','Machine Fragment: Quality Revealer',['chemistry.compounds','economics.market-structures'],22,'An ancient device reveals the true quality of any product, preventing fraud.',_4step('experiment','Test the device with products of known quality levels.','Include high, medium, and low quality samples.','measure','Compare device quality ratings to expert assessments.','Correlation between device and expert ratings.','compare','Compare the device to modern quality testing equipment.','Note which detects more quality factors.','observe','Test whether the device can assess quality of non-physical goods like services.','Present service quality scenarios and check the device response.')),
    ('machine-mkt-currency','Machine Fragment: Universal Exchange',['economics.trade','math.ratios'],22,'An ancient device converts any trade good directly to any other at a fair exchange rate.',_4step('experiment','Exchange several different goods through the device and record the rates.','Test common and rare items in both directions.','solve','Calculate whether the exchange rates are internally consistent.','If A exchanges for B at rate r1 and B for C at r2, then A for C should be r1 times r2.','compare','Compare the device rates to current market exchange rates.','Note whether the device favors any particular goods.','measure','Test whether exchange rates change over time or with supply conditions.','Repeat the same exchange at different times.')),
    ]
    return _quick_biome('marketplace', S, ST)

